<title>JAPAN: Output at big Japan aluminium mills rises in Feb.</title>
<headline>Output at big Japan aluminium mills rises in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Output of fabricated aluminium products at Japan's seven leading mills rose 2.2 percent in February from the same month last year to 127,281 tonnes, according to data submitted by the companies to the Japan Aluminum Federation and released on Monday.</p>
<p>The February data was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Feb 97	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> Total	    127,281	  +2.2 pct</p>
<p> Flat-rolled     99,402	  +0.9 pct</p>
<p>   Can stock     31,398	  -2.9 pct</p>
<p> Extrusions	27,879	  +7.3 pct</p>
<p>The seven companies are Kobe Steel Ltd (includes KAAL, a joint venture with Aluminum Co of America ), Sumitomo Light Metal Industries Ltd, Furukawa Electric Co, Mitsubishi Aluminum Co, Nippon Light Metal Co, Sky Aluminium Co and Showa Aluminum Corp.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
